title ALES13 — Lotus's peak/RMS meter, the same root reading the master
prompt Read REMEMBER + the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design round; send each finished increment; stop at the custody gates.
think Read the two itinerary docs and the custody gates in REMEMBER. Living track is the ALES ladder (Lotus, Season C double-seat) — recent commits climbed ALES8..ALES12. The Lotus README road-on names the next rungs: peak/RMS meter, stereo balance/width, transport loop, choice-of-law.
think Lindy-first crux-first: a meter is the most durable next move — a mixing surface read on every playthrough for years, foundational to any DAW — over the smaller transport loop (only re-drives ALES7) or balance/width (a variation on pan). Its crux is a wider square root: an RMS is isqrt of a mean square, and a full-scale i16 mean square reaches 32768² = 2³⁰, past ALES11's pan-fold isqrt bound of 2²⁴.
think Reuse over copy (the tree's saturate precedent): rather than a second isqrt, widened ALES11's proven isqrt to the audio square domain (2³⁰, sixteen digits) and made it public — power's own inputs stay ≤ 2²⁴, so ALES11's callers and witness are untouched. One root, two readers: ALES11 shapes the field, ALES13 reads the master.
think Two owed truths beyond a bare maximum: rms ≤ peak always (mean of squares ≤ max square, isqrt monotone — asserted at the postcondition), and BLOCK-INVARIANCE (peak a running max, mean-square a running sum, both associative) so metering a master block by block off ALES7's transport equals one whole measure. The second ties the meter to the real read path.
obs GREEN on the first build across seven selftest blocks: silence 0/0; a full-scale constant reads its own magnitude (the i16 minimum landing 32768/32768 at the wide domain's ceiling, exercising the very reason the root was widened); rms ≤ peak across a sweep (a lone spike strictly below, a square wave exactly equal); block-invariance at 1/2/7-sample blocks off transport.read_block; stereo channels metered independently; master never mutated; feed refuses MeterFull leaving the meter untouched.
obs Kept docs synced: refreshed the ALES11 witness Lens line (its old "twelve digits over a 2²⁴ domain" understated the now-widened shared root) and re-ran the power and crossfade witnesses GREEN — nothing downstream of the widened isqrt broke.
obs Custody gates untouched — purely local i16 buffers, no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no real meter hardware. The audio-interface hardware a metered master would feed stays the paused research round.
loom witness=ales_meter_witness result=GREEN rung=ALES13 selftest_blocks=7 isqrt_domain_bits=30 max_meter_samples=67108864
file lotus/meter.rye ALES13 — the peak/RMS meter: a Meter accumulates sum-of-squares, count, peak; rms = isqrt(mean square) reusing power.isqrt; measure / measure_stereo convenience.
file lotus/power.rye widened isqrt to the audio square domain (2³⁰) and made it public + isqrt_max const, so the meter shares the one true root; ALES11's inputs and witness untouched.
file tools/ales_meter_witness.rish witness proving the meter GREEN — silence, DC, rms ≤ peak, block-invariance off the transport, stereo, read-only, MeterFull.
file tools/ales_power_witness.rish refreshed the Lens line to name the shared, widened root honestly (docs-implementation-sync).
file active-designing/20260814-fill-ales13-lotus-meter.md the self-approved design capture for the round.
file lotus/README.md front door synced — ALES13 in the status line, the rung prose, the prove block, and the road-on.
recommend keep-going — the next Lotus rung (stereo balance/width, a transport loop over a marked region, or offering the keeper the choice of pan/crossfade law) is mechanical and single-module, policy already written; custody gates all still untouched.
